<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/050K">Remark <span data-tag="050K">3.1.2.8</span>.</a> Let $f: X \rightarrow S$ be a Kan fibration of simplicial sets. If $f$ is surjective on vertices, then it is surjective on $n$-simplices for every integer $n \geq 0$. This follows from the lifting property of Remark <a data-tag="00UN" href="/tag/00UN">3.1.2.7</a>, combined with the observation that the inclusion map $\{ 0\}  \hookrightarrow \Delta ^ n$ is anodyne (Example <a data-tag="0218" href="/tag/0218">3.1.2.5</a>). </p>
</article>
